+// Makes glTexSubImage2D write the texture storage in place instead of orphaning it
+// (allocating a fresh surface and copying the WHOLE texture over) when the texture
+// was drawn in the last few frames. Big win for apps that stream sub-rects into
+// large textures every frame; the caller accepts that the GPU may sample a mix of
+// old and new texels for a frame.
+void vglInPlaceTexSubImage(GLboolean enable);
